; the pdp64: the grammar of the encoding -- 32 registers (r0-r31).  HAND EDITED.
;
; The master of the encoding grammar: the directives of hbnf and the one include of the parts.  The rules are the parts of spec/grammars.d/ whose `; targets:` line names enc, listed in
; load order by the generated spec/generated/index-enc.hbnf (tools/grammars_d.py): the instruction `insn` (10-enc-insn), the forms and leaves (20-enc-forms, the optimiser's), the operand shapes,
; the vocabulary, the registers and the hot tables, the group mn-ext.  A new instruction family is a new part there (spec/README.md).  `insn` is the first rule (hbnf then reads the grammar as bits).
; Everything the codec, the assembler, the linker, the simulator and the documentation know of this encoding is generated from these parts.

prefix none
include "../generated/index-enc.hbnf"
%start insn
